      "writtenOn": "2022-09-13T15:56:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can skip probing but we can\u0027t skip the i2c enable and unlock. Think about system shutdown and boot, pchg_shutdown() will be called when system shutdown,  pchg_startup() will be called when system boot, the chip is powered off and on so we need to enable i2c and unlock. In this case, the chip_id is set, if we skip i2c enable and unlock, we won\u0027t be unable to access i2c registers. \n\nSo I add the check at line 397 to skip the probing but keep i2c enable and unlock, thought?",
      "parentUuid": "3b550f9e_14e7f631",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 372,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 372,
        "endChar": 32
